From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GE-Proton <git@localhost>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 16:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] winepulse: Split DualSense speaker output from raw haptics

Death Stranding Director's Cut writes controller effects to a four-channel
endpoint. Its float Wwise stream carries controller-speaker audio while a
separate exclusive stream drives the actuators.

Keep the actuator PCM on the raw four-channel path. For the float Wwise stream,
create a private Pulse stream on the controller's public mono speaker sink and
copy hardware channel 1, matching the Linux DualSense UCM speaker route. Feed
that stream when the application releases each render buffer so raw ALSA
availability cannot stall speaker playback. Pace the hybrid endpoint from the
Pulse speaker queue rather than the immediately-consumed raw actuator PCM;
otherwise XAudio renders multiple periods per tick and most speaker samples are
dropped. Clear the speaker pair only from the float raw write to avoid duplicate
playback. Leave the independent 16-bit haptic stream unchanged.

The behavior remains restricted to PROTON_DUALSENSE_SPLIT_AUDIO, leaving the
established Sony controller paths unchanged.
---
--- a/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
+++ b/dlls/winepulse.drv/pulse.c
@@ -93,6 +93,8 @@
 
